how to find a publisher for your book so  i got a great question from my readers  jerry love you guys who wrote in to say  any advice on how to find someone to  publish a book do you have any videos on  this just found out about you a couple  days wow your videos are amazing jerry  clark iii thank you for that compliment  jerry uh buttering up always gets you  onto the show so thank you for that  this is a great question and one that  a lot of people one answer right a lot  of people have a book idea they want to  get it out there they want somebody to  help them market it you realize that you  may be a great writer but not great at  everything else around that you just  want to focus on what you do best so  getting the book deals becoming more and  more difficult the publishing industry  is hurting they're having a hard time  keeping up with online and i wanted to  share my four tips  for you to get your book published  number one is go direct  and going direct is basically finding  all the publishers that publish books  that accept books and and writing to  them and you have a overview of what  your book is all about and you write  into them they usually generally email  address so you can connect with them  sometimes they have  limited dates so they're only accepting  from this date to this date and they're  full up on authors and other times they  they're just always open they say hey  shoot us your proposal there aren't many  publishers who who don't accept in any  format  um but now remember you're gonna go up  against everybody else who's doing the  exact same thing so that that's your  bare basics  entry point is just create an overview  of your book and emailing or mailing out  to all the publishers that you can find  number two is using an agent and with a  literary agent what they do is  dramatically  improve the chance of you getting your  deal they'll look over your proposal  they will  give you feedback suggestions how to  tweak your proposal if you've never done  it before and i'm going through this  process right now it's it's totally  foreign it's totally new and i'm  trusting the people who have experience  in getting big books out and published  and so i'm leaning on their advice to  help  get me that deal now they take a cut of  whatever you make usually you don't pay  a literary agent a fee but they take a  cut or whatever deal they land for you  and so are you willing to give up a  percentage of whatever  you know advance you get  uh in return for getting an increased  chance of getting the book deal for me  it's worth it you know i don't want to  do all that work i don't want to be  emailing all the publishers  and trying to figure it out i'd rather  go with an expert and pay them for that  expertise number three is write great  copy and this  this is so  so so so important because  so many books  are just not that great  they're okay  they're good but they're not great and  if you're a first time author and you  want to stand out and you want to get  noticed the copy has to be great it has  to scream off the page it's got to be  something i look at i have to keep  reading it's a page turner right is your  book actually that  great  and you know show it to friends and show  it to family and show it to complete  strangers and get their feedback on it  and it should be something that is your  life's work  it should be something that you want to  show to your grandkids when it's done  it's got to be that important  it's got to be at that level  because if it's not you're up against so  many people that your chances of being  picked up  are pretty low and if you look at even  some of the most successful books you  look at their history and how they  started even those even though they were  great page turners they still got  rejected  dozens and dozens of times so you have  to make sure that your book is great and  everybody's gonna say my book is great  yeah my book is great so everybody's  saying that right everybody feels the  same way that you do that your book is  great so you've got to take it up a  level it's got to be your life's work if  you only have to write one book ever in  your life this is it and it's got to be  amazing so you've got to pour your heart  soul blood sweat tears everything into  that book  for it to really jump off at me and help  you stand out from a proposal of one out  of thousands that are coming in  and number four is build momentum  the biggest issue now in the publishing  industry is being able to sell these  books right it's easy to produce a book  is getting it sold and so what they want  to see more and more especially from  first time authors is that you have an  audience of some kind you want to build  momentum most authors don't so even if  you have a great book idea the fact that  you have no audience to sell to once  it's out is going to limit your chances  of getting a deal so what you want to do  is start now start building a youtube  audience start building a facebook  audience start building a twitter  audience because if you do that  you're already ahead of most of the  other authors  it gives you a platform  the publishers the literary agents are  going to ask you what is your platform  so they want to know are you an expert  have you gone on radio and tv do you  have a a youtube show do you have people  who follow you on all the social media  networks you have a popular website if  you don't it's going to really limit  your results so start working on those  things now and what i do is think about  what is the core message of your books  you know what is the one word that  defines who you are what's the value  that you want people to to exude what am  i going to learn  from reading your book how is it going  to change me and then create content  around that  so the the content doesn't all have to  be about your book but share with me  things  that make me feel something that are  related to your core philosophy your  core value your one word  and people will gravitate towards that  and when your book is ready to be  launched now you have an audience to  market to so you've got to build  momentum and not just rely on the  publisher to do everything for you  so in summary how to get your book  published number one go direct number  two use an agent number three write  great copy  number four build momentum and believe  it's a great question jerry if you have  something more specific you want advice  on i'm going through this process right  now so i'm happy to help answer it for  you for those of you watching you like  this video you can subscribe to the  channel to see more just like it thank  you so much for watching i'll see you  soon  every week i share my best information  to help you fuel your business forward  in my newsletter check it out below  hi i'm jason j ross fonseca of  risonline.com and i want to say evan  carmichael's newsletter is consistent  fun  inspiring and it's the only newsletter i  prioritize and look forward to period
 

